# Production build (Netlify). DELIBERATELY EMPTY — not a missing value.
#
# The refresh-token cookie is issued with `SameSite=Lax`, so it is only sent on same-site
# requests. Netlify (haytravel.netlify.app) and Azure (…azurewebsites.net) are different
# sites, so calling the backend directly would silently drop the cookie and break the
# silent-refresh/logout flow. Instead `netlify.toml` proxies `/api/*` to Azure, which makes
# every API call same-origin (first-party cookie).
#
# An empty base URL therefore means "hit this same origin with a relative path" — see
# `src/shared/lib/http.ts`, which distinguishes empty (intentional) from unset (config error).
#
# NOTE: a `VITE_API_BASE_URL` set in the Netlify UI overrides this file (Vite gives
# `process.env` priority over `.env` files). It must be removed there for the proxy to apply.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=
